      "question": {
        ":question/id": "44f5ec04-b094-507a-beff-1d5d8144c102",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "Without using a calculator, find the **exact** value.\n\n$$\n\\cos^2\\left(105^\\circ\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(105^\\circ\\right)\n$$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Use the cosine double-angle identity:\n\n$$\n\\cos^2\\left(x\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(x\\right)=\\cos(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstitute the angle and evaluate the standard-angle cosine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\cos^2\\left(105^\\circ\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(105^\\circ\\right) \\\\\n&= \\cos\\left(2\\cdot 105^\\circ\\right) \\\\\n&= \\cos\\left(210^\\circ\\right) \\\\\n&= -\\cos\\left(30^\\circ\\right) \\\\\n&= -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
